# tally 2.2.1 P30 (L §4.4 l.667 to l.671): an operation decides over an interval only what holds for every value
# the interval can hold; its ends stand for them only where it is monotone and gives a value everywhere between.
# The review's k1: a term whose interval's values agree is one value in sum, mean and quantile (days_between(d0,
# wend) * 0: s1's third, m3, q2 print 6, 2, 2, as the engine); a term that varies stays the hole (s1's first). tally 2.2
# held every window term "for a term of".
=== k1.tally
model k1
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source card "invented"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index ks = [a, b, c]
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
input wend: date
input wnext: date
input wover: date
input wmon: date
input wone: date
input wq: date
input wyr: date
input wodd: date
input d0: date
input fxm[m in months]: num
input fxy[y in years]: num
input nm[m in months]: month
input vals[k in ks]: num
input lvl: num
input n5: num
input n28: num
input n30: num
input n31: num
def viam[m in months]: num = fxm[m] + fxm[m]
def viaw: num = viam[wend]
def dbl: num = fxm[nm[wend]]
def gap: num = days_between(d0, wend)
def gap1: num = days_between(d0, wone)
def gapeq: num = days_between(d0, wend) * 0
version v_card
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  wend = window(2026-03-29, 2026-03-31) "c"
  wnext = window(2026-04-01, 2026-04-02) "c"
  wover = window(2026-03-01, 2026-04-01) "c"
  wmon = window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-31) "c"
  wone = window(2026-03-31, 2026-03-31) "c"
  wq = window(2026-03-31, 2026-04-01) "c"
  wyr = window(2026-12-31, 2027-01-01) "c"
  wodd = one_of([2026-03-02, 2026-03-30]) "c"
  d0 = 2026-03-01 "c"
  lvl = 0.5 "c"
  n5 = 5 "c"
  n28 = 28 "c"
  n30 = 30 "c"
  n31 = 31 "c"
  fxm[2026-03] = 4 "c"
  fxm[2026-04] = 5 "c"
  fxy[2026] = 7 "c"
  nm[2026-03] = 2026-04 "c"
  vals[a] = 1 "c"
  vals[b] = 2 "c"
  vals[c] = 3 "c"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "c"
version late
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-03-30
  replace fxm[2026-03] = 40 "c"
ask ke: fxm[wend], fxm[wnext], fxm[wmon], fxm[wone], fxm[wodd]
ask ko: fxm[wover]
ask kq: fxy[wq], fxy[wend]
ask ky: fxy[wyr]
ask kn: viaw, dbl, viam[wend]
ask kk: fxm[wend] as known 2026-03-29
ask kex: explain viaw
ask kch: check fxm[wend] == fxm[wmon]
ask kadd: fxm[add_days(wend, 1)], fxm[add_days(add_days(wend, 1), 1)], fxm[month_of(wend)], fxm[month_of(wover)]
ask m1: mean(vals[k] + gap for k in ks)
ask m2: mean(vals[k] + gap1 for k in ks)
ask m3: mean(vals[k] + gapeq for k in ks)
ask q1: quantile(vals[k] + gap for k in ks, lvl)
ask q2: quantile(vals[k] + gapeq for k in ks, lvl)
ask s1: sum(vals[k] + gap for k in ks), sum(vals[k] + gap1 for k in ks), sum(vals[k] + gapeq for k in ks)
ask mx: max(vals[k] + gap for k in ks), min(vals[k] + gap for k in ks)
ask mxc: max(vals[k] + gap for k in ks) > min(vals[k] + gap for k in ks)
ask me: mean(vals[k] + gap for k in ks where vals[k] > n5)
ask mw: mean(vals[k] for k in ks where vals[k] > gap - n28)
ask ms: mean(vals[k] for k in ks where gap > 0)
ask mh: mean(if vals[k] > 1 then vals[k] else gap for k in ks)
ask cnt: count(k in ks where vals[k] + gap > n30), count(k in ks where vals[k] + gap > n31)
ask am: argmax(vals[k] + gap for k in ks), argmax(vals[k] * gap for k in ks)
=== expect s1 m3 q2
s1: (?"date within window(2026-03-29, 2026-03-31) not precise enough for a term of sum" (wend), 96, 6)
  unknown day: wend
  cut 2026-06-10
m3: 2
  cut 2026-06-10
q2: 2
  cut 2026-06-10
warning: WARN-UNREAD place konto is read by nothing
